{"id":"4bc658a2-f8d4-449c-a22a-04e6cc3daecc","object":"chat.completion","created":1784999607,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    segments = case['segments']\\n    budget = case['budget']\\n    n = len(segments)\\n    # extract fields\\n    names = []\\n    importances = []\\n    minima = []\\n    capacities = []\\n    for seg in segments:\\n        names.append(seg['name'])\\n        importances.append(seg['importance'])\\n        minima.append(seg['minimum'])\\n        capacities.append(seg['capacity'])\\n    total_min = sum(minima)\\n    total_cap = sum(capacities)\\n    if budget < total_min or budget > total_cap:\\n        raise ValueError('Budget out of feasible range')\\n    allocations = list(minima)\\n    remaining = budget - total_min\\n    # While there is remaining budget, allocate to best segment by importance/(next position)\\n    # Keep track of original indices for tie-breaking\\n    while remaining > 0:\\n        best_idx = -1\\n        best_score = -1.0\\n        for i in range(n):\\n            if allocations[i] >= capacities[i]:\\n                continue\\n            # next allocated position = current allocation + 1\\n            score = importances[i] / (allocations[i] + 1.0)\\n            if score > best_score:\\n                best_score = score\\n                best_idx = i\\n            elif score == best_score:\\n                # stable tie: keep the earlier index (first encountered in order)\\n                if best_idx == -1:\\n                    best_idx = i\\n                # else keep original best_idx, which is earlier\\n        if best_idx == -1:\\n            # Should not happen because budget <= total_cap ensures some capacity left\\n            break\\n        allocations[best_idx] += 1\\n        remaining -= 1\\n    # Build by_name mapping\\n    by_name = {names[i]: allocations[i] for i in range(n)}\\n    total = sum(allocations)\\n    return {\\n        'allocations': allocations,\\n        'by_name': by_name,\\n        'total': total\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) for task NLP-LLM-01. The case payload has segments array with name, importance, minimum, capacity; and budget integer. The goal is to allocate budget across segments, starting with minimum quotas, then distributing remaining budget one token at a time to the segment with highest importance/(next allocated position), breaking ties by original order (i.e., the order of segments in the input array). Return allocations (list of integers order matching segments), by_name (dictionary mapping name to allocation), total (sum of allocations, should equal budget if feasible). Validate: budget must be at least sum(minimum) and at most sum(capacity). Raise ValueError if not.\n\nAlso note output structural schema: by_name has dynamicKeysFrom case.segments[*].name, so keys must be exactly the name strings from input segments.\n\nImplementation: iterate segments in order to compute initial allocations = list of mins. remaining = budget - sum(mins). If negative, raise ValueError. If remaining > sum(capacities - mins) also raise ValueError. Then while remaining > 0: for each segment, compute \"score\" = importance / (current_allocation + 1) (since next position would be current+1). But the problem says \"importance divided by its next allocated position\". If current allocation is a, next position is a+1. So score = importance/(a+1). Find maximum. If ties, pick the one with smallest original index (since we process in order and need stable tie break). Then allocate one token to that segment: a+=1, remaining-=1. Check capacity: if current allocation already at capacity, skip? Actually before allocating, ensure not exceeding capacity: we should only consider segments that have not reached capacity. So when computing scores, ignore those at capacity. Also after allocation, we must not exceed capacity;